 C/LDAR:,NAME,
C===========================================================
C C/LDAR - load a non-simple packed field (LSB-ordered struct, or a
C scalar/simple type) addressed through a pointer.
C
C   Entry:  ACC = the field's shift amount (untagged plain integer)
C           M11 = address of the width-specific table (C/01/C/02/C/03/
C                 C/04/C/06/C/07, picked by work.p2c at compile time --
C                 see libc/c_01.madlen)
C           M14 = address of the word(s) containing the field, set by
C                 setAddrTo(14)
C           M13 = return link
C
C prepLoad (work.p2c) selects this over C/RR when the value's kind is a
C scalar, or a struct declared __lsb; C/RR is its MSB/array sibling.
C This is a verbatim port of the Pascal runtime's P/LDAR
C (paslib/p_ldar.dtran); the width-table format it reads via M11 is not
C independently understood beyond the shape documented at c_01.madlen.
C The fixpoint check and full test suite verify it.
C===========================================================
                ,NTR ,3
            1   ,AOX ,11B
           15   ,ATX ,1
           11   ,A*X ,
                ,ATI ,10
           10   ,J+M ,14
           11   ,A*X ,1
                ,YTA ,100B
           15   ,X-A ,1
                ,ATI ,10
           14   ,XTA ,
           10   ,UTC ,
           11   ,ASX ,5
           11   ,AAX ,2
           13   ,UJ  ,
                ,END ,
